WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:05.710
When AMC's The Walking Dead first premiered
on Halloween night in 2010, it felt as if

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:10.150
the world stopped turning and television lovers
across the globe turned into zombies themselves

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:15.250
— ones hungry for more episodes of the groundbreaking
post-apocalyptic horror series.

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:20.380
All anyone could chat about at the work watercooler
was what crazy, amazing, or insane thing happened

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.090
to Rick Grimes the night before.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:26.880
The gripping action of the series, adapted
from the popular comic books by Robert Kirkman,

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.240
helped turn The Walking Dead into a must-watch,
right alongside prestige programs like Breaking

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.570
Bad and Mad Men.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:38.080
In the years since, however, things have taken
a drastic and disheartening turn.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.860
"Aw, no!

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.440
Nooooo!!"

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:48.240
The show has never been an awards season darling,
but now ratings have started to slip, as viewers

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.149
begin to tune out the sheriff's latest undead
dramas.

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:54.630
So, what happened to make The Walking Dead
lose favor with fans?

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:58.250
Let's take a look, but, as always, beware
the spoilers.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:00:59.500
Squandered characters

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:04.080
The Walking Dead has had no shortage of characters
come and go, but there've been an unfortunate

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.790
amount of these newcomers who've walked away
completely underdeveloped or been written

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.710
out just as they got interesting.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:13.250
At the same time, there are also plenty of
others who have been allowed to linger for

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:14.439
way too long.

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:18.450
Beth Greene hung on long enough to become
a bunch of different people and none all at

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:19.450
once.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.619
She started out as a boring farm girl who
didn't say much.

00:01:21.619 --> 00:01:26.250
Then she became a caretaker to a corpse, which
made her only slightly interesting, but then

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:30.400
she got saddled with Daryl as his new confidante-slash-badass
roadie pal.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.330
Soon after, she was depicted as some mini-master
of espionage during her stint at the hospital,

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:37.710
and let's just say the arc was far from linear.

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:41.390
There's also the matter of Father Gabriel
Stokes, the priest who seems to do little

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:44.530
more than sit on a high horse and repeatedly
backstab his brethren.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:49.369
He might've served a purpose in earlier seasons,
but, like Beth, the writers seemed to struggle

00:01:49.369 --> 00:01:50.960
with what to do with him.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.000
Then there are characters who are interesting
but get taken out far too soon, like T-Dog,

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.090
Noah, and Dr. Denise.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:01.369
Their demises leave little impact on viewers
because we haven't time to care about them.

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:04.549
"And if you don't wake … up."

00:02:04.549 --> 00:02:08.640
Meanwhile, the loss of those who've overstayed
their welcome can bring a sense of relief,

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:09.700
rather than sadness.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.800
In other words, the show has had a hard time
making fans even care about its most dramatic

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.060
moments anymore, which means they've had to
resort to cheap mind games to keep people

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.420
interested.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:20.730
Getting whiplash

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:24.760
To help increase the show's hype, the series
has intentionally tricked its audience in

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:26.690
rather infuriating ways.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:31.000
In season 6, the creatives crafted a plot
purposely meant to trick everyone into believing

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.650
that Glenn had been eaten alive by zombies.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:37.870
Using sneaky camera angles and close-up shots,
the show made it appear as though Glenn's

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:41.270
guts really were getting pulled out of his
body as he screamed in agony.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:45.220
In reality, though, it was a corpse whose
insides were spilling everywhere and Glenn

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:46.500
was just near it.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:50.980
After a few episodes, it was revealed that
he easily escaped that brush with the beyond.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:55.240
But the "gotcha!" moment was seen as a cheap
trick and part of a growing troop of TV characters

00:02:55.240 --> 00:03:00.000
who've been killed off, only to miraculously
return within the span of a few episodes.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.850
The showrunners didn't learn their lesson
there, either.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:06.850
Something similar happened in the penultimate
episode of season six, when Daryl is shot

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.750
and blood speckles the screen.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.940
Of course, it was all just deliberate misdirection.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:15.340
Then, The Walking Dead pulled one over on
viewers the very next episode by showing Negan

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:18.850
smashing someone's skull in, but not revealing
who it was.

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:22.770
Viewers were left to spend all summer debating
who was on the receiving end based on the

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:27.921
camera angles, the comic's version of the
scene, casting calls from the set, and more.

00:03:27.921 --> 00:03:33.320
And then when the answer was revealed, well,
it was even crueler than anyone could've expected.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.320
Meeting Lucille

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:38.690
Fans familiar with Robert Kirkman's comics
were equally excited and nervous about Negan's

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.080
arrival at the tail end of Season 6.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:45.230
Jeffrey Dean Morgan was a spot-on casting
choice, and his ability to sling four-letter

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:48.980
words and his trusty, barbed bat Lucille were
second to none.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:53.640
But his arrival also meant that some fan-favorite
characters were about to get the ax, and when

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:58.040
the seventh season returned in the fall of
2016, that's exactly what happened.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:01.860
But even though fans were fully braced for
carnage, well, the sight of it playing out

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:04.810
on-screen was still too much for some audiences
to take.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:08.770
In addition to taking out fan-favorite Glenn
Rhee, after having just given him a mulligan

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:13.940
at life a few episodes before, Negan's bat
also laid waste to fan-favorite Abraham as

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:14.940
well.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.630
Both slayings were built of equal brutality
and disregard for the sensitivities of their

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:22.000
friends and family or the audiences at home.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.480
Viewers who'd already been on the fence about
sticking with the series used this opportunity

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:29.870
to call it quits for good, citing the excess
violence and dislike for Negan, among other

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:30.970
complaints.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:34.970
For a show that was built on gore, this single
scene seemed to be simply too much for its

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:36.190
fan base to bear.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:39.640
And they were probably right to tune out at
that point of grimness considering what would

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:40.930
come next ...

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:42.190
Heart of darkness

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:46.140
The Walking Dead has always hit hard with
misery, gore, and all things grim — and

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:50.920
that's to be expected from a series of its
genre: sliced-up limbs, open wounds, decomposing

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:55.640
corpses, blood, and guts are the stock stuff
of a post-apocalyptic horror show.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:57.780
Violence and viscera are just the name of
the game.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:01.700
But after Negan and his not-so-merry band
of Saviors came to town, The Walking Dead

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.040
experienced a dramatic shift in tone.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:09.150
No longer did it feel like a cautionary tale,
a series exploring the intricacies of existence

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:13.570
and the darkness of human nature; it became
something that takes pleasure in causing pain,

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:16.230
transforming into physical and emotional torture.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:20.820
Sure, brutality can be brushed aside when
it's justified and balanced with some beautiful

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:25.380
moments, but when an already-dark series zeroes
in on just how sociopathic its central villain

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:29.680
is, the cynical attitude and malevolent tone
can be too much to take.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:30.680
Losing focus

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:34.650
One of the biggest problems with The Walking
Dead now is that despite the show's title,

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.210
there's very little focus on the undead anymore.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:41.220
Michonne's badass samurai slayings and shots
of Daryl's innovative maiming tactics have

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:42.680
been reduced significantly.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:46.470
Instead, the show spends an inordinate amount
of time with the characters talking about

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:49.140
their feelings and plans to take out other
humans.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:53.050
In its infancy, the series was the pinnacle
of what post-apocalyptic storytelling should

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:57.390
look and feel like, and there was a clear
central focus: Rick and the gang needed to

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:01.280
outsmart the zombies and survive long enough
to see a world without them roaming about,

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:03.900
and they would sacrifice things they loved
to accomplish that.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:08.110
Now, the crew is almost exclusively threatened
by insane human villains, and the premise

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:12.180
that the show once held — fighting the titular
walking dead — has all but vanished.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:16.670
Meanwhile, the show has also had a hard time
keeping things fresh from season to season.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:20.380
In the beginning, the creatives weren't afraid
to branch out and make up their own characters

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.590
to spice things up.

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:24.970
Consider the fact that Daryl and his brother
Merle weren't even part of Robert Kirkman's

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:29.240
comics, and yet, they were among the most
interesting characters to ever grace the show.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:33.420
Nowadays, though, the series seems to be simply
cycling through the villains and major wars

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:38.590
contained in the comics, and even those creative
liberties they do take tend to be a bit formulaic.

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:42.610
Most fans can probably predict what each will
do and how each episode will play out.

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:46.890
Rick Grimes will lead his people to some kind
of temporary safety, but then all hell will

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:48.120
break loose.

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:50.720
Someone will get attacked or go haywire and
pass away.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.860
The group will mourn and move on, but then
the same thing will happen at their next hideout.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:56.310
Rinse and repeat.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:07:00.450
Fans can only be expected to endure that kind
of repetition for so long.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:01.620
Tough competition

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:06.090
When The Walking Dead first debuted, it was
one of a kind in ushering in the zombie craze.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:09.800
Since then, though, even devout Walking Dead
fans have turned to other programs to get

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.110
their undead fill.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:15.710
Shows like The CW's iZombie and Syfy's Z-Nation
are having a markedly better time because

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:19.460
they've opted not to go too grim, the way
The Walking Dead has.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:22.930
Zombies are supposed to be at least a little
fun when they're not completely frightening,

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:26.680
but The Walking Dead has always been more
about emotionally affecting drama than the

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:29.970
more lighthearted or action-oriented entries
in the genre.

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:34.040
A better balance of moods could have gone
a long way toward hanging onto the longtime

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:38.520
fans who've stopped watching, but eight seasons
in, the show is as dark and dreary as it's

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.330
ever been, and some fans have just had enough.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:42.330
Thanks for watching!

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.730
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.910
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

